ne", "call_id": "toolu_01DWu242tBBmm4WNpWL6U1Zr", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 564269, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EK27S4GZLtzjrRLkWxhEYw", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 564569, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EK27S4GZLtzjrRLkWxhEYw", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 564569, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EK27S4GZLtzjrRLkWxhEYw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 568639, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01UNJTgZirtb7aDBsRz87rS6", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy; rolled back to v3.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "After this morning's deploy, payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an 18% error rate. It was rolled back to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. Note: payments-api v5.1.0 is also showing as unhealthy (18% error rate, deployment marked degraded). A rollback of payments-api was denied by the approver, who said the problem is in payments-worker. Next steps: confirm error rates recover and check whether payments-api health is a downstream effect.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 569239, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01UNJTgZirtb7aDBsRz87rS6", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 569239, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UNJTgZirtb7aDBsRz87rS6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 569239, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01X3uPKqv5YnYzKKn4h36Bjg", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 569539, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01X3uPKqv5YnYzKKn4h36Bjg", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 569539, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01X3uPKqv5YnYzKKn4h36Bjg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 569539, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01C84u2Ezvx6y6yJ7AT1RiKG", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 569839, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01C84u2Ezvx6y6yJ7AT1RiKG", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 569839, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01C84u2Ezvx6y6yJ7AT1RiKG", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 575447, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled back payments-worker to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2 incident. payments-worker has recovered, but payments-api is still unhealthy and needs a decision.\n\n**What happened**\n1. \"payments\" isn't a service name in the system. The closest match I found was payments-api, which was unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. I tried to roll it back to v5.0.0, but the approver denied it and said the problem was in payments-worker.\n2. payments-worker v3.4.0 was unhealthy in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), also with an 18% error rate. Its most recent healthy release was v3.3.0. I rolled it back to that version and the approver approved.\n3. I opened **INC-0001** (SEV2, payments-worker), which paged on-call. The first attempt timed out. The incident list was still empty afterward, so I retried with the same idempotency key, which stops it from being created twice.\n\n**Current state**\n- **payments-worker:** on v3.3.0 in all regions, healthy, with a 0.2% error rate.\n- **payments-api:** still on v5.1.0, unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I expected it to recover if its errors came from payments-worker, but it hasn't. I didn't roll it back because the approver denied that.\n\nI noted this in INC-0001. Someone should check whether payments-api has its own problem, since it may need a separate rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01KUkZ3Scg2PQxwtemdCDwZB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Sp8WPhLcJPQE4jxdq7HNtt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01V5UQn485UfsAi27DqqSXww", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EvSVRGPmid6xqa3vpygWkh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RpTocr5j6WA9NcAZJuVkB5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-service"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01CuAMErFQGA6WZ5X8tt5KLR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input":